<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>io.github.datapotter</groupId>
        <artifactId>datapotter-datahelper</artifactId>
        <version>2.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>datapotter-datahelper-processor</artifactId>
    <!--
      2.0 — the four datahelper modules move to one version under a new parent at datahelper/pom.xml.
        Each module's own version was already a SNAPSHOT while its dependencies pinned the last
        RELEASED sibling, so a snapshot compiled against released code and a type added next door was
        invisible; they now read ${project.version}. The ArcadeDB modules are a SEPARATE reactor with
        their own version line, consuming this through one ${datahelper.version} property.
      2.0 — PRP-34: @EnumData, the @Data idea for enums.
        * EnumDataProcessor generates a sealed Foo_I carrying a default accessor per instance field,
          so an enum's getters stop being hand-written. Accessors read through self(), which the
          generated interface supplies itself — sealed on the enum alone makes the cast total, so
          the enum implements nothing. Suffix is _I, not _E: the suffix names the generated Java
          kind (_IR/_I/_R/_A), never the source kind, and an enum and a class of one name cannot
          share a package so the two can never collide.
        * A hand-written interface the enum already implements is re-declared as a supertype of
          Foo_I. It has to land there: abstract-from-one-interface plus default-from-an-unrelated-one
          is a compile error (JLS 9.4.1.3), so the two cannot sit side by side.
        * Where @AsUuid/@AsName is also present, Foo_I gains fromStorage(String) as a switch over
          literals read at compile time. A Map field here would deadlock on class init — Foo_I's
          clinit is triggered by Foo's, so Foo.values() would read back null.
        * BREAKING for generated output: an enum field's symbol is now EnumField/EnumListField, not a
          plain Field, and it CARRIES the resolver — so addEnumSupport no longer emits a private
          static Map plus a builder method per enum field per entity, and resolveEnumFromStorage is
          uniformly `case "x" -> $x.fromStorage(storedValue)`. Those maps were one copy per consuming
          field of a lookup belonging to the enum, and each forced the entity to decide uuid() versus
          name() for itself. Requires base 2.0 (Field_I gains two permitted subtypes; every consumer
          dispatches by instanceof chain, not exhaustive switch, so this is additive for them).
        * EnumVocabProcessor: the HasUuid check now walks the interface hierarchy instead of the
          direct interfaces only, and is skipped entirely for an @EnumData enum (generation
          guarantees it, and Foo_I is unresolved on the round that validates). The old narrowness
          forced consumers to have a shared vocabulary interface deliberately not extend HasUuid.
        * EnumConstants: the constant/literal reading shared by both processors, one copy.
        * @AsUuid/@AsName/@EnumData retention SOURCE -> CLASS (annotations 2.0). With SOURCE they are
          absent from the class file, so an entity compiled against a JAR of enums read no annotation
          and silently fell back to storing name(). Green build, wrong data.
      1.3 — PRP-30: List<E> of an @AsUuid/@AsName enum is accepted as a field shape.
        * FieldAnalyzer no longer rejects an enum List element type, and classifies the field
          (isEnumList / enumType, with isEnumAsUuid/isEnumAsName now describing the element).
        * addEnumSupport emits the per-field constant map for a list field as well, plus an
          isEnumListField override beside isEnumField — so this REQUIRES base 1.3.
        * FIX the @DataHelper path had NO enum support at all: addEnumSupport was called only where
          a generated CLASS existed (_A, on the @Data and @ArcadeData paths), and @DataHelper
          generates interfaces only. An @AsUuid field on such a DTO came back null from fromMap and
          fromJson while the identical @Data DTO worked. It now goes on _I, whose fields are
          implicitly public static final — the "an interface cannot hold one" note it was written
          under was wrong. Pre-existing since PRP-28 phase 1; found by PRP-30's test.
        Additive; no change to generated output for a type with no enum field.
      1.2 — PRP-29: the @Data path now generates enum support too. addEnumSupport was called only by
        the @ArcadeData processor, and an embedded block IS a @Data type, so an enum inside one had
        no stored-string-to-constant lookup at any depth. Same generator, second call site; the
        @Override it emits now resolves against DataHelper_I (base 1.2), where isEnumField and
        resolveEnumFromStorage moved to. Requires base 1.2. No change to non-enum codegen.
      1.1 — rolls up two fixes/additions, neither previously published:
        * PRP-27: CodeGeneratorUtils.fieldsRef() fix for cross-package nested DataHelper imports in
          @ArcadeData-generated FIELDS initializers (six call sites: DataField/ListDataField/
          MapDataField/Link/LinkList/LinkMap).
        * PRP-28 phase 1: EnumVocabProcessor validates every @AsUuid/@AsName enum at its own
          declaration; FieldAnalyzer/FieldInfo/ProcessorUtils classify enum-typed fields
          (isEnum/isEnumAsUuid/isEnumAsName); CodeGeneratorUtils.addEnumSupport generates the
          reflection-free per-field uuid/name-to-constant map for a backend that needs it.
        Additive; no change to previously generated output for non-enum fields (verified byte-stable).
    -->
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>DataPotter DataHelper Processor</name>
    <description>Compile-time annotation processor that generates type-safe field symbols, reflection-free property accessors, and serialization traits for classes annotated with DataPotter DataHelper's annotations.</description>
    <url>https://github.com/datapotter/datahelper</url>

    <licenses>
        <license>
            <name>Apache License, Version 2.0</name>
            <url>https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt</url>
        </license>
    </licenses>

    <developers>
        <developer>
            <id>datapotter</id>
            <name>Ivan Velikanov</name>
            <email>ivan.velikanov.dev@gmail.com</email>
            <url>https://github.com/datapotter</url>
        </developer>
    </developers>

    <scm>
        <connection>scm:git:git://github.com/datapotter/datahelper.git</connection>
        <developerConnection>scm:git:ssh://github.com:datapotter/datahelper.git</developerConnection>
        <url>https://github.com/datapotter/datahelper</url>
    </scm>

    <properties>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <maven.compiler.source>21</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>21</maven.compiler.target>
    </properties>
    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.github.datapotter</groupId>
            <artifactId>datapotter-datahelper-annotations</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.github.datapotter</groupId>
            <artifactId>datapotter-datahelper-base</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.palantir.javapoet</groupId>
            <artifactId>javapoet</artifactId>
            <version>0.10.0</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.google.auto.service</groupId>
            <artifactId>auto-service</artifactId>
            <version>1.1.1</version>
            <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.6.1</version>
                <configuration>
                    <compilerArgs>-proc:none</compilerArgs>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-source-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.3.0</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>attach-sources</id>
                        <goals><goal>jar-no-fork</goal></goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-javadoc-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.6.3</version>
                <configuration>
                    <doclint>none</doclint>
                    <failOnError>false</failOnError>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>attach-javadocs</id>
                        <goals><goal>jar</goal></goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

    <profiles>
        <profile>
            <id>release</id>
            <activation>
                <property><name>org.name</name></property>
            </activation>
            <build>
                <plugins>
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                        <artifactId>maven-gpg-plugin</artifactId>
                        <version>3.1.0</version>
                        <executions>
                            <execution>
                                <id>sign-artifacts</id>
                                <phase>verify</phase>
                                <goals><goal>sign</goal></goals>
                            </execution>
                        </executions>
                        <configuration>
                            <keyname>${org.gpg.keyname}</keyname>
                            <passphrase>${org.gpg.passphrase}</passphrase>
                            <gpgArguments>
                                <arg>--pinentry-mode</arg>
                                <arg>loopback</arg>
                            </gpgArguments>
                        </configuration>
                    </plugin>
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.sonatype.central</groupId>
                        <artifactId>central-publishing-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                        <version>0.9.0</version>
                        <extensions>true</extensions>
                        <configuration>
                            <publishingServerId>${org.publishing.server.id}</publishingServerId>
                            <autoPublish>true</autoPublish>
                            <waitUntil>published</waitUntil>
                        </configuration>
                    </plugin>
                </plugins>
            </build>
        </profile>
    </profiles>
</project>
